* BLDC motor electromagnetic subcircuit
*
* A B C  = three-phase motor terminals
* W      = mechanical speed port: 1 V = 1 rad/s
* TOUT   = electromagnetic torque output: 1 V = 1 N*m
* params: Ke=0.0418 Rs=0.50 Ls=200u pp=4 theta0=0


.subckt BLDCMOTOR A B C W TOUT 
* Normalized trapezoidal back-EMF waveform, -1 to +1
.func trap(x) {limit((3/pi)*asin(sin(x)),-1,1)}

* Back-EMF sources
BEMFA EA N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0))}
BEMFB EB N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0)-2*pi/3)}
BEMFC EC N V={Ke*V(W)*trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0)+2*pi/3)}

* Phase windings
LPA A LA {Ls}
RPA LA EA {Rs}

LPB B LB {Ls}
RPB LB EB {Rs}

LPC C LC {Ls}
RPC LC EC {Rs}

* Numerical reference for the floating wye neutral
RREF N 0 1G

* Electromagnetic motor torque output
BTORQ TOUT 0 V={Ke*(trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0))*I(RPA)+trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0)-2*pi/3)*I(RPB)+trap(idt(pp*V(W),theta0)+2*pi/3)*I(RPC))}

.ends BLDCMOTOR